      "informal_statement": "For a nonempty type $\\beta$, a function $f : \\alpha \\to \\beta$ is eventually constant along a filter $l$ on $\\alpha$ if and only if there exists an element $x \\in \\beta$ such that $f$ tends to $x$ along $l$ with respect to the principal ultrafilter at $x$."
    },
    {
      "full_name": "tendsto_atTop_of_eventually_const",
      "formal_statement": "Formal Name: tendsto_atTop_of_eventually_const | Kind: theorem | Type: ∀ {X : Type u} [inst : TopologicalSpace X] {x : X} {ι : Type u_2} [inst_1 : Preorder ι] {u : ι → X} {i₀ : ι},\n  (∀ i ≥ i₀, u i = x) → Filter.Tendsto u Filter.atTop (nhds x) | Path: Mathlib.Topology.Neighborhoods",
